                  <provenance type="#c"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_458">Reading, Berkshire.
                        Benedictine abbey of Saint Mary the Virgin</orgName><p>Written, admirably,
                        on strong paper by a scribe who signed himself 'Abyndone'. Additions by him
                        at the end consist in the acta of the chapter of Reading in 1410 and 1414
                        and decrees of Abbot Thomas Earley promulgated in 1410. The main body of the
                        text contains also two formulary documents relating to
                     Reading.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">The binding of s. xvii/xviii bears the
